{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_w6oha23hmibwajhoea5dmu5j7lxcapdrpivfapochnecln36kzzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation is byte-exact against the C — no divergences found, and `src/lib.rs` needed no changes** (md5 identical before/after).\n\n## Results\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | 5/5 symbols, **0 missing**, 0 unresolved (`ldd -r`), both profiles |\n| Phase B — `CONFIGS.md` rows 1–28 | 27 tests, all pass (row 28 = feature combos, in `verify.sh`) |\n| Phase C — `ERRORS.md` rows 1–28 | 28 tests + 1 sanity check, all pass |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no `add_executable`, no `[[bin]]` |\n| All feature combinations | No `[features]` table; default + `--no-default-features` × debug + release = 60/60 green in each |\n\nThe prior translation was already correct on the three things most likely to break: the `(int)` cast of out-of-range/NaN doubles (C uses `cvttsd2si` → `INT_MIN`; Rust's `as` *saturates*), f64-precision division, and NaN falling through `fabs(data) > 0.000001` to the *else* branch.\n\n## Two false-pass traps I found and closed\n\nWorth flagging, since both initially made broken code look green:\n\n1. **`cargo test` does not rebuild a `cdylib`.** My first mutation run reported 60/60 green for six deliberately broken versions of `lib.rs` — the tests were loading a stale `.so`. Closed with `assert_fresh()` in the harness (refuses to run on a stale artifact) plus always building first in the scripts.\n2. **libtest writes its own progress text to fd 1**, which landed inside the stdout capture window under parallel threads. Closed via `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` and flushing both Rust's and libc's stdout before redirecting.\n\n## Negative control (`./mutate.sh`)\n\nGreen tests are only meaningful if they go red on a wrong translation, so I mutation-tested the suite: **10/10 mutants caught** (saturating cast, threshold shift, format-string bug, NaN→0, `floor` vs `trunc`, wrong constant, label typo, f32-precision division, inverted NULL guard, `%u` vs `%d`). One mutant survives *correctly* — `>` → `>=` at the `1e-6` threshold is a provable equivalence, since no `f32` widens to exactly `1e-6`.\n\nArtifacts in `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `verify.sh`, `mutate.sh`, and 4 test files (60 tests). `c_src/` untouched apart from the `build/` directory."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1034,"cache_read_input_tokens":110490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1034,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15229670-5305-41e5-914f-7a824d2fa62f","uuid":"adc84ed5-785e-43c8-ad47-44731f66c82d","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:49:55.457Z"}
